full":"Solaris Resources Inc. engages in the acquisition, exploration, and development of mineral properties. It focuses on exploring copper, molybdenum, gold, lead, zinc, and silver. It owns interests in Warintza project located in southeastern Ecuador in the province of Morona Santiago, Canton Limon Indanza; and the Tamarugo project located in northern Chile. The company also holds interests in the La Verde project located in the Sierra Madre del Sur west of Mexico City in Michoac\u00e1n State, Mexico; and the Capricho and Paco Orco projects in Peru. In addition, it has an option agreement to acquire up to a 100% interest in 10 new explorations concessions; and has an option to acquire up to a 100% interest in a new portfolio of exploration areas (\u0093Solaris 2\u0094) located immediately adjacent to the Warintza Project in southeastern Ecuador. The company was formerly known as Solaris Copper Inc. and changed its name to Solaris Resources Inc. in December 2019. Solaris Resources Inc. was incorporated in 2018 and is headquartered in Baar, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew Charles Rowlinson | President, CEO & Director | Age 41","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 84 people. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Solaris Resources Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $1.1B market cap.","Returns on capital run at -21592% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, thin -6.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 41% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-3.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Basic Materials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 597% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Solaris Resources (NYSEAMERICAN:SLSR) Share Price Breaks Below 50-Day Moving Average \u2013 Here\u2019s Why","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/solaris-resources-nyseamericanslsr-share-price-breaks-below-50-day-moving-average-heres-why.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794397396.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of SLSR and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/150/Behavioral_Patterns_of_SLSR_and_Institutional_Flows_110826011802_1794118682.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794118682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (SLSR)","source":"news